WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.500
Timing matters. Is now a good moment?

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:12.400
Nobody announces that their customers just got unhappy.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:20.400
Barnwise put its price up a quarter in May.

4
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:27.000
Customers look around after a price rise. That is a window, and it has a date.

5
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Freshroute publishes nothing about what it changed.

6
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.700
And it lists where it looked. So you know they are quiet, not that we missed it.

7
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:49.700
Six people asked for a different price list per restaurant.

8
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:56.600
Nobody sells that. It is the closest thing to customers telling you what to build.

9
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:01.300
Taken from the middling reviews, not the angry ones.

10
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:07.900
Furious people describe their day. Lukewarm ones describe the missing feature.

11
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.900
What people are saying is next.
